# AppSizes & Responsive UI

`AppSizes` lives in `lib/core/extensions/app_sizes.dart`. It is a **BuildContext extension**, not a static token class. Feature screens must consume it. Do not add ScreenUtil, another sizing package, or a parallel token system.

Reference design: **360×800**. Scale design values through the extension.

## Use this

```dart
padding: context.spaceHorizontal(16)
padding: context.spaceSymmetric(vertical: 16, horizontal: 20)
SizedBox(height: context.height(16))
width: context.width(120)
borderRadius: context.circularRadius(12)
```

Also available: `context.getWidth` / `getHeight`, `availableHeight`, `isSmallScreen`, `isLandscape`, `addHorizontalSpace` / `addVerticalSpace`, `spaceVertical`, `spaceAroundAll`, `fromLTRB`, `spaceTop` / `spaceBottom` / `spaceStart` / `spaceEnd`.

Typography: `context.font16Bold` (and siblings) from `text_style_extension.dart`. Colors: `context.colors`.

## Do not

```dart
padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 20)
const SizedBox(height: 16)
width: 350
height: 200
AppSizes.horizontalPadding  // does not exist
```

Prefer `width: double.infinity` plus padding/constraints over fixed screen sizes. Combine with `MediaQuery`, `LayoutBuilder`, `Flexible`, `Expanded`, `FractionallySizedBox`, `ConstrainedBox`, `SafeArea`.

`LayoutExtensions` (`.pad()`, `.padTop()`, …) use **unscaled** values. Prefer `context.space*` / `context.width` / `context.height` for production layout.

## Hardcoded values

Allowed only for a truly unique visual (illustration offset, OCR overlay, one-off animation). Extract to a named local constant (`const _illustrationOffset = 17.0`). If the value is reusable, add it to `AppSizes` in core instead.

## Before any UI work

1. Read `lib/core/extensions/app_sizes.dart`.
2. Reuse existing core extensions (sizes, text, theme).
3. Extend `AppSizes` only when a reusable dimension is missing.
4. Never redefine sizing inside a feature.
